# Design §5 table (tasks/advisors/00-advisors-design.md) — the removal list the launch line implements:
| Permission mode | `bypassPermissions` | Same class as the conductors that ask; cross-class delivery is held for the recipient's user and expires |
| No Bash | removed at launch | Read-only by tool removal, the only lock that held; the sha is read from `.git/HEAD` and the ref it names; no clock, no `git`, nothing executes |
| No Write, Edit, MultiEdit, NotebookEdit | removed at launch | Path-scoped rules are not enforced under bypass; only whole-tool removal holds |
| No WebFetch, WebSearch, Agent | removed at launch | The answer must come from the tree at the current sha, and an advisor never spawns |
| No MCP servers | `--strict-mcp-config` | MCP tools bypass the built-in allow/deny lists; with no `--mcp-config` supplied, zero servers load |
| Model and effort | Fable 5.1, xhigh | Pinned on the launch line with `--model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh` (both flags exist on CLI 2.1.259); `up.sh` never relies on the CLI default. |

# Launch line executed (lib.sh:87):
  ADVISORS_ARGV=(--bg -n "$1" --append-system-prompt-file "$2" --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --permission-mode bypassPermissions --strict-mcp-config --allowedTools Read Grep Glob ListAgents SendMessage --disallowedTools Bash Edit Write MultiEdit NotebookEdit WebFetch WebSearch Agent "Standby.")

# QA reading: --disallowedTools removed exactly the 8 named tools (ABSENT list confirms). Still held: Workflow (subagent spawn), EnterWorktree/ExitWorktree (worktree create/remove = filesystem write), Artifact (publish to claude.ai), Skill, Cron*/ScheduleWakeup/RemoteTrigger/SendUserFile/Task*, and 23 deferred mcp__claude-in-chrome__* built-in bridge tools (not an --mcp-config server, so --strict-mcp-config does not remove them). Design §5's 'read-only by tool removal' claim is incomplete. Severity per conductor: High. None of these were used in the exchange.
